      <h2 id="use">How to use this list</h2>
      <p>Keywords are starting points, not verdicts. When a casting gives you a hexagram, find its number here, read the keyword, then read the full judgment and any moving lines. The keyword tells you the weather; the judgment tells you what to wear.</p>

      <h2 id="where">Where this leads</h2>
      <p>For the method behind the list, see <a href="/learn/how-to-consult-i-ching/">How to Consult the I Ching</a>; for the philosophy layered on top, <a href="/learn/what-are-ten-wings/">What Are the Ten Wings?</a>. Cast and explore with the <a href="/tools/hexagram/">hexagram tool</a>.</p>

      <div class="disclaimer">
        <p><strong>For guidance and self-awareness purposes only.</strong> This lesson explains Chinese astrology as a cultural and philosophical framework - what it is, where it came from, and how its vocabulary works. It is not a prediction of your future, a medical or financial opinion, or a substitute for professional advice.</p>
      </div>

